                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "1f9ea834-594e-43b6-9052-af379ce8ef59",
                        "entry_id": "22c1efa8-89b7-31e3-8e8c-9bcba880c675",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "orogénèse"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "74c3b49f-3017-34f3-99c4-9bcd7931474f",
                        "entry_id": "22c1efa8-89b7-31e3-8e8c-9bcba880c675",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Phase de formation des montagnes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9dc3c4d-9e6e-4805-9ae6-6ab7b3ddd983",
                                "sense_id": "74c3b49f-3017-34f3-99c4-9bcd7931474f",
                                "text": "Le long de la partie orientale du Groenland, au nord du cercle polaire, affleurent les formations géologiques formées durant l’orogenèse calédonienne (du nom latin « Caledonia » pour l’Écosse)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0bf90ab1-1bf6-3233-bce9-c20e905336f9",
                        "entry_id": "22c1efa8-89b7-31e3-8e8c-9bcba880c675",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Système théorique expliquant les mécanismes de formation des reliefs."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d753f698-ae14-40a2-8c10-4a0495d32dfa",
                                "sense_id": "0bf90ab1-1bf6-3233-bce9-c20e905336f9",
                                "text": "Ce livre présente trois divisions principales : oroplastique, étude et description des inégalités de la surface terrestre, saillies ou dépressions telles qu’elles frappent nos sens; orométrie, mesure des reliefs tant pour leur hauteur précise que pour leur masse; orogenèse, étude de l’origine des montagnes et des causes qui en ont déterminé la formation."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fef35778-bcc1-43d9-8e7f-5183eb193544",
                        "source_entry_id": "22c1efa8-89b7-31e3-8e8c-9bcba880c675",
                        "target_lang_word": "Gebirgsbildung",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Gebirgsbildung",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "254f530d-78e9-32e6-ad3d-a3a048d9e59e",
                                        "entry_id": "f6d1ac99-d5a7-374a-879c-753c393df1ad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Bildung/Entstehung von Gebirgen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Orogenese"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f08dda4d-0261-4a30-9fa0-5582ef3576ef",
                                                "sense_id": "254f530d-78e9-32e6-ad3d-a3a048d9e59e",
                                                "text": "„Neben die Gebirgsbildungen tritt ein weiteres wichtiges geologisches Ereignis, das Eiszeitalter, in dem Nordeuropa mehrfach von einer mächtigen Inlandeisdecke überdeckt war, die sich bis nach England, nach Mitteleuropa und in das Osteuropäische Flachland hinein erstreckte.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d45b5294-4924-44c8-98de-db7df3d9ab6b",
                        "source_entry_id": "22c1efa8-89b7-31e3-8e8c-9bcba880c675",
                        "target_lang_word": "orogeny",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "orogeny",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f9119229-dc73-33b6-88fd-8968e99fec4d",
                                        "entry_id": "8b896a7b-b27d-3056-953a-725aaaf7288e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The process of mountain building by the upward folding of the Earth's crust."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cac2c76c-f419-49c9-81d7-99ba30f85579",
                                                "sense_id": "f9119229-dc73-33b6-88fd-8968e99fec4d",
                                                "text": "Coordinate term: taphrogeny"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f56c45a3-483b-472c-bfbe-0b2c700cba19",
                                                "sense_id": "f9119229-dc73-33b6-88fd-8968e99fec4d",
                                                "text": "The effects of Acadian orogeny are concentrated in central Newfoundland, decreasing in intensity to the east and west (Williams, this volume)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6857dda-e40e-4a99-a534-acc68b159a04",
                                                "sense_id": "f9119229-dc73-33b6-88fd-8968e99fec4d",
                                                "text": "When I asked Geoff Milnes what age the rocks were before they were turned into uncompromising gneisses by the Alpine orogeny he made a rueful face."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28b7f2d0-4fd0-4067-96f6-4b1d46bda93e",
                                                "sense_id": "f9119229-dc73-33b6-88fd-8968e99fec4d",
                                                "text": "In Canada the fold-thrust belt formed during what is termed the Columbian orogeny (Monger and Price, 2002). Because the Sevier and Columbian orogenies were contemporaneous and constitute a single continuous and linear belt of rocks and structures, I use the term Cordillera orogeny to refer to the Cretaceous deformation that created the entire belt, whereas the term Laramide is used only to refer to a series of Late Cretaceous—Tertiary basement-involved uplifts, for the most part located in the Rocky Mountain foreland east of the fold-thrust belt and mainly south of the Lewis and Clark lineament (Fig. 1) in keeping with the original definition by Armstrong (1968)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
